# Profy Changes Log

## 2026-10-07 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 12)
- P1 quadratic candidate generation (6a72a6f): follows of glued copies led
  back to matches other copies had already reached, and each was re-judged
  ("twat" * 320: 51,360 reading evaluations vs 3,240 at 80 copies; 640 copies
  1.43s, x13 per x4; "shit-ass", "dickwad", "twaat" likewise). Each raw match
  is now judged once per expression and pass (`seen` in check()); a raw span
  fully determines its readings and follows, so this changes no result.
  "twat" * 640: 0.13s, x3.7. Regression test over 7 shapes (plain,
  stretched, stretched end, long, mixed entries, hyphenated entry,
  separator; r12 x10.9-14.7, now x3.7-4.0).
- P2 boundary readings: "bitttchhell" gave "********ell" (r11 masked all):
  the leading-run trim only split runs of three or more, so "hell" [7,11)
  was never a reading after "bitttch". The trim now splits any run of the
  first letter (up to _GIVE_BACK_LIMIT), and a trimmed reading (`_Reading.
  before`) only counts next to a chosen reading ending where it starts (it
  gets the left need in every alternative), so a double that is the word's
  own invents no compound ("git|tite", "wop|pish"). Trailing splits at both
  sides were tried and dropped: two split readings of one double supported
  each other ("git|t|tite").
- Junction sweep ($S/junction.py: 6,000 random pairs of bundled English
  entries A+B with A's last letter = B's first, the junction letter doubled
  and tripled, 11,998 texts): r12 11,540 fully masked, now 11,991; 451
  fixed, 0 broken; the 7 left need a run longer than the give-back limit
  ("peeenusssss...").
- Differential vs r12, all 40 corpus runs: 0 lost, 0 gained, 1 mask grown
  ("cockknobbing"), 4 match changes ("fuck|knob" instead of "fuckk|nob").
  Sweep: identical (789). Dictionary scan: 845, identical set and masks.
  Windowed/compacted vs full rescan: 0 diffs (65,903 texts x 3 x 4).
  Timing vs r12: throughput and tiny checks within 1%; adversarial worst
  cases +3-5% ("* " * 200 English 0.42s -> 0.44s, all languages 0.82s ->
  0.85s), every scaling ratio ~x4.

## 2026-10-07 (fix/codex-review-hardening, match-selection redesign + Codex review pass 11)
- Selection redesign (Codex pass 10 assessment): check() no longer accepts
  candidates one at a time in expression order. Per pass, every finditer()
  match of every expression yields readings (`_readings`): the match, the
  give-back reading for a copy that follows (`_end_before_profanity`, now
  tried on the raw match before the bleed guards, and followers may hold
  whitespace: "soltar pedoss|oltar pedos"), readings starting later in a
  stretched run of the first letter ("as|sshit"; a double is the word's own:
  "git|tite"), and the copies such readings free (follows). The bleed guards
  judge each reading (`_unbled`: cross-word retry, joined-word cut); the
  per-reading guards (elision, hex, Scunthorpe, false positives) in
  `evaluate`; a reading the Scunthorpe guard protects keeps its
  `_chain_needs` alternatives. `_select` then picks the non-overlapping set
  by DP over the readings sorted by start (4 states: a supporter ends here /
  the reading ending here still needs its right neighbour), linear in the
  number of readings. Order: reported letters+digits, letters+digits,
  reported and all characters that spell something (letter symbols; not
  whitespace or separators no letter stands for), fewest matches, expression
  order, start offsets; one big-int score per set.
- Deleted: contained()/replace() takeovers, `_Accepted` records, owners
  array, pending/pending_lengths/deferred, `_resolve_chains`, the give-back
  takeover by prefix entries and other spellings (`_ExpressionInfo.takeovers`,
  `expressions_of`, prefix tuples and cache), the in-word replacement guard,
  the hex re-check after shortening, the separate "clos|clos" branch (folded
  into `_end_before_profanity`), `_CandidateFinder._full`,
  `_Dictionary.unelided` (now in `_ExpressionInfo.elision`) and `_ordering`.
  core.py 1249 -> 1220 statements, 520 -> 498 branches; check() 202 -> 90
  statements (the bleed guards moved to `_readings`/`_unbled`, unchanged).
  Measured and kept: `_DISCARD` (without it +290 fragment matches across
  separators inside words, "verdam-mt"), the confirming pass (single pass:
  sweep failures English 524 -> 1996, Spanish 2 -> 57).
- Guards the selection needed: a reading starting inside a word and crossing
  whitespace is a fragment when the part in that word has fewer than two
  letters/digits or nothing after the whitespace holds a letter
  ("cabron|a $Naa" as asna, "nichon|s* Nson" as con, "shit|s hit",
  "bourrin|es @" as ecu; greedy order used to hide these); main and r11
  agree on every such example.
- P2 (Codex pass 11) literal block entries vs longer matches: block hits are
  candidates (expression number -1, exempt from guards) the first pass must
  cover (`required`), by themselves or by a containing reading; readings
  overlapping one only partly are left out (`splits_a_hit`). A containing
  reading is the one reported. Hits a shortened run folds together are
  merged into one hit as the most severe entry ("$" * 14, block "$$$","$$").
  "n!gger" block "!" at extreme: extreme match; "ass hole" block "ass":
  asshole; "a!ss" block "!" at high: the entry's own "!".
- P2 (Codex pass 11) long block entries vs stretched words: block entries no
  longer feed `_RunShortener` (their text is found before shortening);
  property test with random letters and lengths up to 300.
- Latent hang fixed (custom expressions only, r11 too): an empty cross-word
  retry restarted its follow at the candidate's own start.
- Intended test changes: `test_a_containing_match_keeps_the_more_severe_report`
  -> `test_overlapping_readings_prefer_reported_then_covered_characters`
  ("whooore" is one moderate "whore" by default; still "w******" at high);
  `_resolve_chains` unit tests -> `_select` tests (same scenarios, plus
  tie-breaks and required coverage); KNOWN_REPEAT_FAILURES 14 -> 3 (all three
  fail in r11 too).
- Differential vs r11 (HEAD 101c9df), all 40 corpus runs: 0 lost; 33 gained
  (all cross-language, German "zu" read from "**u" where r11 already reported
  "po" on the "**"); native masks 139 grown (mostly inflected compounds:
  "fuckbitching", "tittyfuckers"), 19 shifted, 3 shrunk (r6 "cockass -
  cockass" no longer masks the " - " between copies; one split-corpus tie).
  Sweep (excluding ordinary doubles) r11 -> now: English 960 -> 524, German
  373 -> 232, French 255 -> 31, Spanish 14 -> 2 (1602 -> 789).
  Dictionary scan: 845, identical set and masks. Windowed/compacted vs full
  rescan: 0 diffs over 65,903 texts x 3 strategies x 4 languages.
- Timing vs r11: prose throughput and tiny-check latency within 1%;
  adversarial worst case "* " * 200 English 0.39s -> 0.43s, all languages
  0.76s -> 0.83s (budget 2s); scaling ratios all ~x4. Hot `re.*` calls in the
  per-candidate guards are precompiled; a raw match inside a hex-like token
  is skipped before its readings are generated.

## 2026-10-07 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 10)
- P1 takeover leak: the give-back takeover (`base, expression = entry`)
  rebound the expression loop's variables, so later matches of the scanned
  expression were judged as the taking-over entry ("slutslut sluts" clean at
  minimum_severity="high"; "slutslut slutsmith" masked "slutsmith"). Queued
  candidates now carry their own entry and expression; the loop variables are
  `scanned_base`/`scanned` and never rebound. Reviewed check() for other
  outer state rebound in nested branches: none (start/end/matched_text,
  retry, info and token are per candidate).
- P2 exact block entries vs normalization: explicit block entries are matched
  as literals (case-insensitive, any whitespace) on the visible input before
  normalization and run shortening, judged by the exact-entry predicate on
  that text (`is_exact_visible`), and accepted with their original spans at
  the start of the first pass, ahead of every heuristic. Hits whose letters a
  shortened run folded into an earlier hit's ("0" * 12 for "00") are reported
  with their own spans and take nothing in the working text. The in-loop
  predicate became unreachable and was removed. Fixes German "Fischhändler",
  "schhh" and Spanish "carrrro".
- Simplifications (Codex): full-scan dispatch only in
  `_CandidateFinder.candidates()` (full mode returns before any lookup);
  accepted matches kept in per-pass records (`_Accepted` with a `standing`
  flag) and survivors appended at the end of each pass, replacing the global
  `withdrawn` set. Proof: r10 plus only these two changes vs r10: 0 differing
  results (masks and match metadata/order) on all 40 corpus runs, identical
  sweep failures (29070 texts) and dictionary scan.
- Final vs r10: corpora 0 diffs (none contain block entries); sweep 6 changed
  outputs, all the takeover leak ("titti-titti": later copies were masked
  although each copy alone is clean); dictionary scan identical (845);
  windowed/compacted vs full scan 0 diffs. Tiny checks +65us (the extra
  method call per expression), text throughput unchanged.

## 2026-10-07 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 9)
- Invariant sweep ($S/sweep.py): every bundled entry not a false positive,
  plain / one interior letter tripled / a rarely doubled letter doubled / one
  leet substitute, repeated 1-4x with "", " ", "-", ",": every character of
  every copy must be masked. Doubling an ordinary letter makes a different
  word by design ("cook", "good"); reported separately, not part of the
  invariant. Failing texts outside that class, r9 -> now: English 5583 ->
  960, German 7733 -> 373, French 2971 -> 255, Spanish 1357 -> 14.
- P2 repeated profanities ("twattwat", main too): `_end_before_profanity`
  gives back up to 3 trailing characters when the same expression, another
  spelling of the word, or an entry the word starts with matches from there
  (on a slice: the start guard refuses starts inside the first letter's run),
  or, inside a run of one letter, a literal profanity runs to the word's end
  ("shitt|its"; not "gitt|ite"). The following copy goes on a per-candidate
  stack. Wildcards ("*") are never given back; slices are bounded by 4x the
  match length. Any other shortened candidate (cross-word retry, joined-word
  retry) re-tries the expression in the freed letters (`follow_from`).
- P2 pending chains vs shorter overlaps ("baastard" * 3): a candidate
  overlapping a longer pending one is deferred until chains are resolved.
- Same-pass replacement: a candidate strictly containing this pass's accepted
  matches replaces them when it starts at a word edge and none is more
  severe (exact block entries always do): "fuccckd", "fagggt", "shhits".
- Cross-word fixes the sweep exposed: a match that starts inside a word and
  runs through separators into the next is discarded (`_DISCARD`: "ha|ji-had|
  ji", "tu|sh-t|ush"); a hyphenated dictionary word before the separator
  counts as the plain word ("shit-brain|-s"); a stretched word before it is
  matched against the entries the base starts with ("sluut,s|luut"); the
  dictionary-word exception needs the left word to cover the plain part; a
  tail of letters or digits after any symbols, or of substitutes after
  separators no letter stands for ("\ick|,\|ick"). Glued phrases: a
  phrase embedded at one end may continue into a profanity or the same
  expression; at both ends only when both neighbours are profanities.
- Multi-letter keys: per-letter variant expressions for entries using them,
  processed before the multi-key expression of the same entry; German "sch"
  spelled s, optional c, h (normalization turns "sch" into "sh"); Spanish "rr"
  kept whole; German normalization `s+c+h+` -> "sh", Spanish `r{2,}` -> "r".
  Per-expression data (first characters, wildcards, elision, takeovers) is
  computed once (`_ExpressionInfo`).
- Seeded property test (150 entries, 4 languages) with an explicit list of
  14 known residual failures, plus regression tests for each class.
- Differential vs pass 8 (r9), all corpora x 4 languages: native 0 lost,
  0 smaller masks, 689 gained, 415 masks grown; cross-language 258 lost
  (spurious short-word fragments across inserted separators inside foreign
  words), 95 gained. Windowed/compacted vs full scan: 0 diffs. Dictionary
  scan: 845, identical set and masks.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 8)
- P2 chain alternatives: `_chain_needs` returns every minimal alternative
  (left, right, both) instead of the first; `_resolve_chains` keeps a
  candidate while any alternative's sides are supported (same linear support
  counting). "bitchhbiitch", "damnnbiitch", "bitchhbiitchhfuck" are caught.
  Keeping all alternatives exposed chains the arbitrary choice used to drop:
  supporting candidates must now be entries of 3+ letters
  (`_COMPOUND_PART_MINIMUM`, as for compound parts: German "su|spek" read as
  zu|speck in "xsuspekty"), and an elided candidate needs a word edge or a
  match on both sides ("sht|dck" yes, "sangreeroot"'s "ngr|eeroo" no).
- P2 one predicate for explicit block entries (`is_exact_block` in check()):
  judged on the visible input (original minus invisible characters, before
  normalization and run shortening): the case-folded, whitespace-collapsed
  match text equals the entry and neither edge continues an alphanumeric
  token, or the alphanumeric token around it is the entry repeated (per-token
  root length cached per check). It holds before every heuristic and skips
  them all (cross-word bleed and retry, joined-word cut, elision, hex/UUID,
  Scunthorpe/compound/chains, false positives); replaces the hex-only
  exemption. Fixes "-12345678", "12345678-", "-deadbeef1-"; "ab" in
  "ab12cd34ef" and "ab8ab8ab8" (an obfuscated form) stay protected; "abab"
  with block=["ab"] is now masked (entry repeated).
- Property test `test_a_block_word_with_any_separators_masks_its_own_text`:
  1050 entries (hex-like, digit-only, mixed-case, plain, spaced cores x every
  separator, space and ZWSP/ZWJ/VS16 before, after, around, inside, doubled)
  in one filter per driver; r8 fails 12 (regex). Random entries now draw
  from every separator too.
- Distinct-match hex scaling test resized to 3000 vs 12000 (r7 x10.6, now
  x4.3; 3.9 under coverage stayed below the 5s ceiling at the old size only
  barely).
- Differential vs pass 7 (r8), all corpora x 4 languages: 0 lost, 7 gained
  (6 English consonant-only compounds spanning the word: ccksck, shtdck,
  shtcnt, sckdck, bttbng, nggrdng; 1 cross-language), no mask changes.
  Windowed/compacted vs full scan: 0 diffs. Dictionary scan: 845, identical.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 7)
- P2 joined-word cut vs compounds: "ass-holefuck" was cut to "ass", leaving
  "fuck" protected inside "holefuck" (unchanged at minimum_severity="high").
  `_joined_word_cut` keeps the longer match when the letters after it start
  another profanity (`_starts_with_profanity` over `compound_parts`); the next
  profanity then abuts a match and counts as a compound. Results equal pass 5
  (r6) for ass-holefuck/-bitch, sh-itfuck, fu-ckshit, cock-suckerass at every
  severity level; hell-Lloyd, shit-tom, ass-Sasha stay apart.
- P2 hex exemption with distinct matches in one token: replaced the
  per-(token, match) verdict cache with a per-token summary (case-folded text
  and its shortest repeated unit, `_root_length`, KMP prefix function, linear
  on 3.9 too); `_repeats(folded, root, unit)` is O(len(unit)): the unit must
  be a whole number of roots, divide the token and start it. 16000 distinct
  "ab"/"8" matches: 4.08s (x11.4 per 4x) -> 0.58s (x4.1); regression test.
- Differential vs pass 6 (r7), all corpora x 4 languages: 0 lost, 0 gained,
  2 mask changes (split French "ass:ssassin(s)" under the English filter,
  back to the pass-5 mask). Windowed/compacted vs full scan: 0 diffs.
  Dictionary scan: 845, identical to passes 5 and 6.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 6)
- P1 word-gap retry was quadratic: `_WORD_GAP` re-ran from every position of
  a long symbol run ("h e l" + "!£" * 8000: 3.2s, x10 per 4x). Gaps are now
  the maximal `\W+` runs holding whitespace (`_NON_WORD_RUN`), scanned once:
  0.58s, x4. Regression test at 2000 vs 8000 units (old x10.4, limit x8).
- P1 hex exemption compared the whole token per match: verdicts are cached per
  (token span, lowered match) within a pass (`is_whole_block_token`).
  block=["12"] alone on "12" * 64000: 2.46s -> 0.24s; test at 32k vs 128k
  chars for "12", "1212", "deadbeef1" (old x10.6-12.1).
- Per-match audit (each probed at 4k vs 16k chars, all ~x4): word-gap retry
  (fixed above), hex exemption (fixed above), hex verdicts (cached per token),
  `_is_spanning_word_boundary` and its retry (O(match), bounded gap count),
  chain resolution (`_resolve_chains`, linear support counting), compound and
  Scunthorpe guards (context cut to the window), false positives (length
  check before slicing), `_modifies_previous` (each selector run walked once),
  `_original_span`/claims (O(match)), the new joined-word cut (one anchored
  regex, side words bounded by the longest entry) and elision check (C-speed
  letter count, early exit).
- Joined words ("hell-Lloyd" -> "*******oyd", main too): a match shaped plain
  word + symbols + letters that ends inside the next word, not on an
  inflection, is retried on the plain word (`_joined_word_cut`); if only
  another entry spells it ("shit-t|om" as "shitt"), the candidate is dropped.
  Not when the symbols stand for letters (the profanity must match without
  them: "lust**g|e"), nor when both sides form a dictionary word, with or
  without the letter repeated around the separator ("cock*k|blocker").
- Elision ("*Lloyd" -> "***oyd", main too): a match that only exists without
  the vowel (checked against the expression compiled without the elision
  option) needs one letter or specific substitute per non-vowel position
  (`_spells`, `_spelling_characters`; "*" is accepted by every letter of
  "hell", "$" only by "s"; German "ck" is one position).
- Differential vs pass 5 (r6), all corpora x 4 languages: native corpora 0
  gained; lost only 8 (German, "d**el"-style consonant + two "*" read as an
  unrelated elided word); cross-language runs lose 601 such coincidental
  short-word hits. Native masks mostly grow to the whole word ("k*ck").
  Windowed/compacted vs full scan: 0 diffs. Dictionary scan: 845, identical.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 5)
- P2 cross-word retry at any separator: a candidate rejected for running into
  the next word is re-matched before each gap between words in it, last gap
  first, cutting before the gap's symbols and then at its spaces
  (`_retry_before_word_gap`, `_WORD_GAP`); "hell - Lloyd", "hell / Lloyd" and
  every other bundled separator now give "**** <sep> Lloyd".
- P2 run shortening redesigned as one mechanism (`_RunShortener`, replaces
  `_shorten_runs_with_mapping` and `long_run_pattern`): characters are grouped
  by a signature over every letter class, separator set, literal and "\w"
  the expressions use (case-insensitive, as they match), so "uUüÜ" is one run
  in English; literal characters and characters a multi-character option
  repeats (German "ck", "ss") only run with their own case variants; the
  first and last character of a run are kept. Only runs of letter-class
  characters are shortened ("-" * 8 and emoji runs are matched as they are).
  Kept length per class: the bundled words' old floor, the class's own word
  and option runs (a block word "x" * 300 no longer keeps "u" runs at 300),
  8 for hex digits (the hex guard sees identifiers at their length), and
  congruent to the run length modulo every literal run of the character with
  the cut on a multiple of it, so complete literal occurrences stay complete.
  Tokenization moved to `_tokenize` (cached) for reuse.
- P2 hex guard: a hex-like token made only of an explicit block word, once or
  repeated ("12121212" for "1212", "0" * 12 for "00"), is exempt (`_repeats`).
- P2 invisible characters in entries: regex-driver block/allow entries drop
  invisible characters like the text (blank afterwards = ignored; the literal
  driver keeps entries as typed), and variation selectors and emoji tag
  characters after a match are masked with it (`_modifies_previous`).
- Empty character classes (a dictionary without letters, e.g. only
  block=["--"] after allowing every bundled word) compile to "(?!)".
- Differential vs pass 4 (r5): every corpus x every language (36 runs) 0
  lost / 0 gained / 0 mask or match changes; targeted corpus (mixed-case
  stretched bundled words, profanity + separator + next word): 0 lost.
  Windowed/compacted vs full scan: 0 diffs over 3060 texts x 2 x 4 languages.
  Dictionary scan: 845 flagged, identical set and masks.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 4)
- P2 rare-double chains: protected candidates that would qualify with a
  profane neighbour are kept pending (`_chain_need`) and resolved per pass by
  a linear support-counting fixpoint (`_resolve_chains`); accepted via a shared
  `accept()` closure.
- P2 block words vs hex guard: a blocked entry that is the whole hex token is
  exempt. Property test gains hex-like/all-digit/digit+letter shapes.
- Confirming-pass windowing (`_CandidateFinder`): each generated expression
  gets a stop class (`_compile_profanity`); an attempt at p reads only
  [p - 1, first stop char]. Confirming passes reuse the previous pass's
  matches outside zones around masked spans and search zones with an exact
  endpos bound, or scan a compacted copy (\x01 runs collapsed) when masks are
  dense; short texts (< 512 chars) and unknown expressions scan in full.
  Equivalence vs the pre-windowing engine: 0 diffs over ~66k texts per
  strategy (windowed, compacted, default) in all 4 languages. Stops are keyed
  by id() (Pattern.__hash__ re-hashes the compiled program: 1.8us per lookup).
- Timing (default filter): "shit "*32000 8.09s -> 6.63s; 100k clean text with
  5 matches 0.99s -> 0.50s; README prose 10k/100k and clean 100k unchanged.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 3)
- P1 per-match mutation: masks are applied once per pass (`_mask_spans`),
  same-pass claims use a bytearray, original-coordinate claims a bytearray,
  run indexes are rebuilt per pass (removed `_RunIndex.split` and `_claim`).
  One-word filter "shit "*512000: 79.6s -> 4.0s. Default filter "shit "*32000
  stays ~7.9s: ~95% is one regex scan per entry per pass (pass 1 ~5.2s, the
  confirming pass ~2.4s over 160k chars); Python bookkeeping ~0.7s.
- P2 block words match themselves: split runs keep separators later literal
  tokens need, entries collapse whitespace, blocked entries win length ties,
  pattern driver uses (?<!\w)/(?!\w) edges and \s+ for spaces; literal
  expressions are cached per word (`_compile_literal`). Property test over a
  curated set plus 300 seeded random words, both drivers.
- P2 phrase-break retry: a candidate rejected for crossing a phrase break is
  re-matched with the text cut before the break ("hell, Lloyd").
- P2 rare doubles in compounds: per-side edge rule (`_ends_with_profanity`,
  `_starts_with_profanity`) plus abutment with accepted matches
  (`touches_before`/`touches_after`).

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, Codex review pass 2)
- P1 quadratic scanning: `_RunIndex` (bisect over `\w`, hex and letter runs,
  built once per check and split on masking), cached hex-token verdicts
  (`_is_hex_token`), bounded before/after windows for the substring guard,
  bounded next-word lookahead, `\x01`/bisect overlap checks, single-pass mask
  assembly; dropped the per-pass whitespace re-collapse (provably a no-op) and
  the identity copy of the position map. "a55"*4000 17.6s -> 0.48s,
  "shit"*4000 33.6s -> 0.8s; all shapes now ~4x time per 4x length.
  Removed `_full_word_context`, `_alpha_word_context`, `_is_inside_hex_token`.
- P2 inflections: full suffix set incl. y -> i forms (`_INFLECTION_SUFFIXES`,
  `_Y_ENDINGS`, `_is_inflection`): y-endings need a doubled consonant or a
  y-adjective entry; an ending may start with the stem's repeated last letter.
- P2 obfuscated plurals across a phrase break: allowed when the next word is
  a stem of 2+ letters or single letters plus an inflection.
- P2 compound guard: `_is_pure_alpha_substring(matched, before, after, ...)`
  receives the letters around the actual occurrence.
- Dictionary scan: 830 -> 845 flagged (15 y-adjective forms such as cockily,
  smuttiness; 0 newly clean).
- Coverage: moved the claimed-span overlap check into `_claim` (CPython 3.9
  did not trace the `continue` after a multi-line condition).

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening, round 2 + Codex review pass 1)
- Doubled letters: `_RARELY_DOUBLED` (a h i j k q u v w x y; each doubled in
  <0.5% of /usr/share/dict/words entries containing it, next letter d at 1.7%)
  marks deliberate stretching when the match is the whole word or the word plus
  an inflection, so `fuuckin`/`shiit` are caught while `vacuum` stays clean.
  Added `shiite`/`shiites` to global false positives.
- Match bleed: `_is_spanning_word_boundary` rejects matches that run into the
  next word across phrase punctuation (`shit, s|aid`), counts only tokens
  mixing letters and symbols as obfuscation (`fuck - you|rself`), and lets a
  match stop inside the next word only before an inflection (`@ss hole|s`).
- Compound rule in `_is_pure_alpha_substring`: another profanity must abut the
  match (`hell|fuck`); `ero` anywhere in `zerowi` no longer disables the
  Scunthorpe guard for `dth` in `zero\u200bwidth`.
- Dictionary scan: 2355 (original) -> 1318 (round 1) -> 830 flagged; newly
  flagged vs round 1: bastaard, naziism.
- Codex P1: identical adjacent letters may keep a run split by separators
  (`coo-on`, `pimm-mel`, `cell*lule`; space only if the letter repeats after it).
- Codex P2: run shortening keeps per-character spans and matches never share
  original characters (`"💩"*8` with a callback mask deleted the rest of the text).
- Codex P2: named groups/backreferences (`\100` was parsed as octal, so block
  words needing >99 groups never matched).
- Codex P3: overlapping-severity test for the pattern driver.

## 2026-10-06 (fix/codex-review-hardening)
- ReDoS: rewrote expression generation in `profy/core.py` (`_tokens_expression`
  and helpers). Each letter run is committed through an atomic group emulated
  with `(?=(...))\N` (Python 3.9 compatible), shared characters such as `*`
  stay in a run only when one of its own letters follows, gaps only take
  separators the next letter cannot start with, a start guard skips positions
  inside the first letter's run, inner runs are bounded (64 chars / 32 steps)
  and runs of one character longer than any dictionary word needs are
  shortened for matching only (span-mapped). `"*" * 22` went from ~29s to
  ~2ms; scans are linear in input length (500-char adversarial inputs from
  every bundled separator/substitution character: worst ~0.3s with all
  languages). Differential run against the previous engine over ~25k
  generated obfuscations: detection identical except 6 exotic
  multi-separator forms. Compiled expressions are cached per profanity.
- Scan loop never accepts zero-length matches; blank allow/block entries are
  ignored (fixes `filter_text("!", block=[""])` hanging).
- Combined-language dictionaries merge only accent/diacritic substitutions
  (port of Blasp `Dictionary::forLanguages`), fixing "sock" in english+german.
- Block list keeps existing severities (Blasp semantics), overrides bundled
  false positives for the exact word; allow still wins over block.
- Unknown/empty language selections raise `ValueError`.
- Repetition expansion: `_is_pure_alpha_substring` protects matches that only
  exist through ordinary double letters (cook/cookie/good); 3+ repeated
  letters remain deliberate. /usr/share/dict/words scan (234,456 words):
  2355 flagged before, 1318 after, 0 newly flagged.
- Added `driver="pattern"` (port of Blasp `PatternDriver`).
- Invisible characters are stripped only for matching with a span map back to
  the input; `original` is the exact input and `clean` only masks matches.
- One-shot helpers use a bounded `lru_cache` of compiled dictionaries;
  expressions are pre-sorted once per dictionary.
- Sync tooling: `sync_from_blasp.py` pulls only per-language word lists into
  `sources/upstream/`, `sync_external_sources.py` stores normalized source
  candidates in `sources/external/`, and the new `scripts/wordlist_layers.py`
  assembles `profy/data/languages/*.json` (byte-identical to the previous
  bundle: english 2663 profanities). Removed PHP implementation hashing;
  metadata/report only change with upstream; added `--check`.
- Release workflow: version consistency check, derived prerelease flag, wheel
  smoke test in a clean venv, publish only on tags, no skip-existing.
- CI: Python 3.14 added; tests reorganized (test_detection, test_options,
  test_unicode, test_redos, test_internals, test_sync_scripts) with 100% line
  and branch coverage enforced via pytest-cov.

